# unseen-attention-configs -- curated attention problems deliberately NOT present
# in tier1-attention-configs, used to measure generalization to never-encountered
# problems (quick-tuning / ML-classifier coverage on out-of-distribution shapes).
# Each line fully specifies -t and the four trans flags so it maps to exactly one
# problem (the attention loader otherwise expands unspecified -t/trans flags).
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored by the config loader.
#
# Novelty is anchored on axes tier1 never exercises:
#   * split_kv > 1 (flash-decoding)            -- tier1 is split_kv 1 everywhere
#   * num_heads_q != num_heads_kv (GQA / MQA)  -- tier1 is 1/1 everywhere
#   * with-attn-scale / with-attn-bias = true  -- tier1 never sets these
#   * return_lse = true                        -- tier1 is false everywhere
#   * head_dim_qk != head_dim_v (MLA-style)    -- tier1 always has them equal
#   * fresh head dims / long context / bf16 on tier1-only-f16/f32 shapes

